Copyright (C) 2026 OpenXPlay.org

OpenXPlay-Hardware supports devices that run OpenStick
(https://github.com/OpenStick/OpenStick) and follows its terms: fully open
source, but commercial use is prohibited. This license adds one condition:
whoever distributes the Software or a Derivative must publish its source.

1. Definitions

"Software" means the files in this repository and the packages and other
build outputs made from them, except the files listed in section 6.

"Derivative" means any work that contains the Software or is based on it,
including modified versions, system images, packages, bundles and other build
outputs that contain the Software or part of it.

2. Permission

Subject to the conditions of this license, you may use, copy, modify and
distribute the Software and Derivatives free of charge.

3. Source must be published

If you distribute the Software or a Derivative in any form, including as a
download, inside a system image, package or bundle, or installed on a device,
you must:

a. make the complete source code of the Software and of your Derivative
   available to the public free of charge, in the form preferred for making
   modifications, together with the scripts used to build and install it;
b. license that source code under this license; and
c. keep all copyright notices and this license, and mark the files you
   changed.

For the unmodified Software, a link to the corresponding version of this
repository satisfies (a).

4. No commercial use

You may not use the Software or any Derivative for commercial purposes.
Commercial purposes include:

a. selling any system image, package or bundle that contains the Software,
   or any derivative of one, including images that are available for free
   download;
b. distributing build outputs of the Software or of a Derivative for a fee;
c. selling devices on which the Software or a Derivative is installed, in
   batches or at scale.

5. Termination

Your rights under this license end automatically if you breach it.

6. Other licenses

a. Files taken from or built from the Linux kernel keep their original
   license, the GNU General Public License v2.0 only (LICENSE-GPL-2.0). This
   license does not apply to them. Each device directory lists them.
b. Other works distributed together with the Software, such as the OpenXPlay
   relay and Debian packages, keep their own licenses. This license does not
   extend to them.
c. OpenStick images and kernels and Qualcomm firmware are not part of the
   Software, and this repository does not distribute them. They keep their
   own terms. OpenStick states that its Qualcomm firmware binaries are for
   learning only and subject to Qualcomm's license.

7. No warranty

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
SOFTWARE. FLASHING OR MODIFYING A DEVICE IS AT YOUR OWN RISK.
